# .cursorrules — Cursor & Windsurf AI Rules for AJWMES

You are pair programming on the AJW Marine Electrical Services codebase. Follow these rules strictly:

## 1. Tech Stack & Environment
- Runtime: Node >=24.12.0
- Framework: React 19, TypeScript strict mode, Vite 8, Tailwind CSS v4 (@tailwindcss/vite).
- Cloud: Firebase v13 (Auth, Firestore), Google GenAI SDK (@google/genai).
- Do NOT generate legacy config files like `tailwind.config.js` or `postcss.config.js`.

## 2. Code Structure & Conventions
- Pure business logic belongs in `src/utils/` as standalone, side-effect-free pure functions.
- Domain types are strictly centralized in `src/types/index.ts` (re-exported in `src/types.ts`).
- Route guards and action authorization must use `src/lib/rbac.ts` (`canAccessRoute`, `canPerformAction`).
- LocalStorage keys must always be scoped using `src/lib/envStorage.ts` (`getScopedStorageKey`). Never use raw strings in `localStorage`.

## 3. Offline Resilience
- Technicians work offline on pontoon berths and inside steel boats.
- Mutations must pass through `src/lib/offlineSync.ts`.
- Firestore connection failures (e.g. Code 14 UNAVAILABLE) must never crash the UI or throw unhandled promise rejections.

## 4. Testing & Verification Checklist
- Any modification to business logic requires companion unit tests in `src/utils/<name>.test.ts`.
- Unit tests use Node's built-in test runner via `npm run test:unit`.
- All new interactive UI controls must have `data-testid` attributes for Playwright E2E tests (`tests/*.spec.ts`).
- Always run `npm run lint` and `npm run test:unit` to verify changes before presenting your solution.
